      "visible":true,"showLabel":true,
      "data":{"identity":{"graphId":"handoff-graph-rendering"},"markdown":"## Conversion boundary\n\nThe useful experiment is **semantic fidelity**, not visual fidelity. Twilite should preserve stable object identity, meaningful labels/content, semantic relationships, meaningful hierarchy/grouping, useful source references, and provenance.\n\nTwilite should reinterpret visual presentation, node views, semantic zoom, ports/handles, navigation, expansion, graph membrane placement, and editing behavior.\n\nThe strongest result is not a Handoff clone. It is a Handoff graph that clearly becomes native Twilite structure after crossing the boundary.\n\nSaving edits should produce a Twilite document rather than pretending to round-trip Handoff perfectly."}
